# REGENT OF BANGKA

# PROVINCE OF BANGKA BELITUNG ISLANDS

# COPY

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANGKA REGENCY

# NUMBER 9 OF 2019

# CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

# REGENT OF BANGKA,

Considering:  
a. that women's empowerment is carried out so that women can actualize their potential optimally to participate in development in accordance with their nature and capacity;  
b. that women as national assets who play a role in the process of succession and preparation of quality generations, need to receive guarantees of their rights and protection from acts of violence and discrimination in order to build society, nation and state;  
c. that based on the provisions of Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, mandates that women's empowerment is a mandatory affair organized by the Regency Regional Government;  
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Protection;  

In View of:  
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;  

2. Law Number 28 of 1959 concerning Stipulation of Emergency Law Number 4 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1956 Number 55) Emergency Law Number 5 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1956 Number 56) and Emergency Law Number 6 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1956 Number 57) concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions including Kotaparaja Within the Level I Region of South Sumatra As Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1959 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1821);  
3. Law Number 27 of 2000 concerning the Establishment of Bangka Belitung Islands Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 217, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 4033);  
4. Law Number 1 of 1974 concerning Marriage (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1945 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1974 Number 1, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3019);  
5. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);  
6. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);  
7. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);  
8. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);  
9. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635), as amended by Law Number 31 of 2014 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5601);  
10. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);  
11. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4967);  
12. Law Number 36 of 2009 concerning Health (State Gazette Year 2009 Number 144, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5063);  
13. Law Number 19 of 2011 concerning Ratification of the Convention On The Rights Of Persons with Disabilities (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 107, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5251);  
14. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5589) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);  
15. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);  
16. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in Regions as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 67 of 2011 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in Regions;  
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 1 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Improving the Quality of Life of Women;  
18. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Women's Protection;  
19. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 4 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Empowerment of Community Institutions in the Field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;  

With Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BANGKA REGENCY and

# REGENT OF BANGKA

# DECIDES:

To Establish: REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION
